# Where the designer reaches its API. Baked in at `npm run build`.
#
# Leave it unset for anything single-origin, which is the normal case:
#   * `npm run dev`      — the Vite proxy forwards /api and /help to :8000
#   * the container      — nginx serves this build and proxies /api beside it
#   * `python -m process_engine_api` serving designer/dist itself
#
# Set it only when the designer is served from a different origin than the API —
# a static host, a CDN. Use the API's public base URL, no trailing slash:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://engine.example.com
#
# The API must then be told where the designer lives, so SSO logins and
# run-notification links point back to it (env vars on the API host):
#
#   PROCESS_ENGINE_PUBLIC_URL=https://engine.example.com     # the API's own origin
#   PROCESS_ENGINE_DESIGNER_URL=https://designer.example.com # this app's origin
#
# Prefer the single origin. Cross-origin works — auth is a bearer token in
# localStorage, not a cookie, so there is no credential handling to get wrong —
# but it is one more thing to keep in step.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=
